.TH ORO-NATIVE 3 "" "Oro Runtime" "Oro Runtime API Manual"
.SH NAME
oro:native \- JavaScript API module
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
import * as module from 'oro:native'
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Calls explicitly configured compiled Android extensions through the runtime's document\-owned IPC. No JavaScript module or executable path is loaded natively.
.SH REFERENCE
.TP
\fBrequest(extension, action, payload, options)\fR
Invokes a narrowly named native operation with a JSON object payload. Requests require a foreground interactive document, expire after 90 seconds and share native capacity limits. Results are limited to 512 KiB. The extension must implement its own feature authorization; trusted origin is not server IAM. Unregistered extensions and other platforms reject with ENOSYS.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIextension\fR (string; required) Configured extension name.
.br
\fIaction\fR (string; required) Operation name.
.br
\fIpayload\fR (object; optional)
.br
\fIoptions\fR (NativeRequestOptions; optional)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<any>\fR
